ut eight points at the presidential level. He cleared his primary easily and enters the general election with a massive financial advantage, roughly $6.8 million on hand, over state Senator David Brock Smith, who raised about $121,000 and has drawn no meaningful outside spending.\n\nNo public general-election polling exists, but every major race rater labels Oregon Safe or Solid Democratic, and prediction markets give Merkley a 96 to 98 percent chance of winning. The main uncertainty is the size of the margin rather than the outcome, with a potentially competitive governor's race in Oregon the one sign of a favorable Republican environment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9939, "margin": 17.74}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9912, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.994, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9925, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9912, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9935, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9932, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9932, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9944, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9936, "margin": 18.0}]}